fields.description:
Create a new asset with specified configuration and dependencies.

Example Usage:
```graphql
mutation {
    asset {
        create(input: {
            k8sTaskConfig: {
                taskUuid: "01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef"
                cluster: "prod-cluster"
                parameters: [
                    { key: "ENV", value: "production" }
                ]
            }
            name: "data_processor"
            upstreamDependencies: [
                { assetId: "raw_data_asset_id", delay: "PT30M" }
            ]
        }) {
            asset { 
                id 
                name
            }
            wasCreated
        }
    }
}
```

Update an existing asset's configuration and dependencies.

Example Usage:
```graphql
mutation {
    asset {
        update(input: {
            id: "existing-asset-id"
            name: "data_processor_v2"
            k8sTaskConfig: {
                taskUuid: "updated-task-uuid"
                cluster: "new-cluster"
            }
        }) {
            asset { 
                id 
                name 
            }
            wasCreated
        }
    }
}
```

Delete an asset from the system.

Safety Check: The asset can only be deleted if it has NO downstream dependencies.
This ensures the dependency graph remains valid and no assets are left with broken upstream references.

Example Usage:
```graphql
mutation {
    asset {
        delete(input: {
            assetId: "01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef"
        }) {
            deletedAsset {
                id
                name
            }
            wasDeleted
        }
    }
}
```

