fields.description:
Submit a new task for execution with specified configuration and retry policy.

You can run a task in two ways:
1. **Direct Task Config**: Provide k8sTaskConfig with explicit configuration
2. **Asset-Based**: Provide assetId to run a pre-configured asset with optional parameter overrides

The task will be queued for execution and you'll receive a TaskRun with ID
to monitor progress. Task will automatically retry on failure based on retryCount.

Example Usage (Direct Config):
```graphql
mutation {
    runTask(input: {
        k8sTaskConfig: {
            taskUUID: "data-processing-job-v2"
            cluster: "prod-us-west-2"
            parameters: [
                { key: "INPUT_PATH", value: "s3://data/input.csv" }
                { key: "OUTPUT_PATH", value: "s3://data/output/" }
            ]
        }
        retryCount: 2
    }) {
        taskRun { id status }
    }
}
```

Example Usage (Asset-Based):
```graphql
mutation {
    runTask(input: {
        assetId: "01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef"
        parameters: [
            { key: "INPUT_PATH", value: "s3://custom/input.csv" }
            { key: "BATCH_SIZE", value: "500" }
        ]
        cluster: "prod-us-west-2"
        suppressDownstreams: false
    }) {
        taskRun { id status assetId }
    }
}
```
